# What never reaches the Docker build context.
#
# The context is the repository root, because the control-plane image needs
# three workspace packages and the lockfile that pins them (see the header of
# apps/control-plane/Dockerfile). Everything below is either rebuilt inside the
# image, belongs to a different deployment profile, or must not be in a build
# context at all.

# Installed and generated trees. A host `node_modules` carries Windows
# junctions and platform-specific binaries; a host `dist` would let a stale
# local build silently become the image's, which is the one class of bug a
# container is bought to remove.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
apps/hq/src-tauri/target
apps/hq/src-tauri/gen
packages/protocol/v3

# Every environment file, including the examples. The image bakes no
# configuration: secrets arrive as container environment at run time, so nothing
# here needs one, and a context that cannot carry a `.env` cannot leak one into
# a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local.json
# Carries real shoot-machine mount paths; no COPY names it, this keeps it out
# of the BuildKit context entirely.
apps/file-bridge/bridge.config.json

# The desktop and web profiles. Neither is containerized: `apps/hq` would put a
# second copy of the RPC surface behind the same contract (ADR 0009), and its
# static export needs no server at run time (ADR 0005).
apps/hq/public
apps/hq/tests
apps/hq/src-tauri
apps/file-bridge/src

# Repository furniture with no bearing on a build.
.git
.gitattributes
.github
.husky
.vscode
.claude
.agents
docs
shared
**/*.md
